      "writtenOn": "2022-05-16T23:49:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The NetworkOffer is essentially an \"offer\" to CS to bring up a NetworkAgent. This means that the offer should exist as long as the interface exists (and is up) because that when we could bring up a NetworkAgent. Stopping a network / unregistering a NetworkAgent should not affect the offer (connectivity is still there if CS decides to use it).\n\nI think I am answering my own question here, unregisterNetworkOffer *must* be called when an interface is removed or goes down. For some reason I remember that being a little painful, but cannot directly recall what the issue was. Let me take another look.",
